<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
        <TargetFrameworks>net10.0;net11.0</TargetFrameworks>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
        <Title>CliInvoke</Title>
        <Authors>AlastairLundy</Authors>
        <Description>Run external processes in C# without System.Diagnostics.Process footguns. Mockable abstractions, DI, and middleware included.</Description>
        <Copyright>Copyright (c) Alastair Lundy 2024-2026</Copyright>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/alastairlundy/CliInvoke</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
        <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>#### Added
- Multi-targets `net10.0` and `net11.0`; on `net11.0` the platform control adapters use the new .NET 11 `Process` APIs (`Process.Signal`, `TryWaitForExitStatus`, `TryGetProcessById`). Windows and macOS children start suspended and resume only after the configured `ProcessResourcePolicy` is applied.

#### Changed
- Validation rule predicates are nullability-honest: `ProcessResultValidator`'s predicate-based constructor and `AddValidationRules` now accept `Func<TProcessResult?, bool>[]`, matching the documented null-input contract for validation rules. Erased CLR signatures are unchanged.
- `CliInvoke` adopts `Squash` (2.1.0) build-time trimming. The IL linker now strips unreachable non-public code from the shipped assemblies at Release build time; the public API surface is untouched. Measured as of this release: CliInvoke.dll for net10.0 TFM shrinks ~37% (218 KB → 138 KB) and the package as a whole shrinks ~15% (311 KB → 264 KB) - the removed code is almost entirely unreferenced Polyfill-emitted types.
- `Polyfill` bundling moved here from `CliInvoke.Core` (which is now dependency-free)
- `CliRun.FireAndForget(ProcessConfiguration)` fails fast on redirected configurations (`ArgumentException` before start) - the handle is disposed immediately after launch, so redirected pipes would never be drained.
- `ExternalProcess` resolves `TargetFilePath` once at construction; an unresolvable path now throws `FileNotFoundException` there instead of at start, and repeat starts reuse the resolved path.
- Retry middleware rewinds seekable standard input (`Position = 0`) before every retry attempt; a non-seekable stdin source throws `InvalidOperationException` when a retry would occur.
- `LoggingMiddleware` logs the joined `ArgumentList` when the argument string is empty.
- Updated `Microsoft.Extensions.*` dependencies to 10.0.14.

#### Fixed
- Raw-mode invocations no longer deadlock on chatty children: `OutputRedirection` is forced off before start in `InvocationMode.Raw` (caller configuration untouched).
- Buffered cancellation is deterministic: a drain-side `OperationCanceledException` is absorbed under `CancellationThrowsException=false` and propagated when `true`.
- Wait paths poll for actual child exit after a forceful kill, so `ExitCode` is readable immediately after a kill-timed-out wait.
- `AllowExceptionsIfUnexpected` no longer swallows genuine failures that resolve near an expected timeout - only CliInvoke's own cancellation `OperationCanceledException`s are absorbed.
- Null environment-variable values reach the child process for removal instead of being dropped by the control adapter.
- `ProcessResult.Signal` is correct on the `net11.0` Unix leg: raw native signal numbers are mapped through the platform table before the SIGKILL and unknown-signal filters.
- `LoggingMiddleware` argument redaction works again (`RegexOptions.ExplicitCapture` had broken capture references, emitting the redaction marker with the wrong formatting).</PackageReleaseNotes>
        <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>true</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>MPL-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <PackageVersion>3.2.0-alpha.1</PackageVersion>
        <AssemblyVersion>3.2.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
        <PackageTags>shell,command-line,cli,automation,execute,executable,wrapper,powershell,cmd,timeout,cancellation,standard-input,standard-output,standard-error,invoke,process,invocation,execution</PackageTags>
        <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
        <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
        <IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
        <PackageId>CliInvoke</PackageId>
        <Product>CliInvoke</Product>
        <PolyEnsure>true</PolyEnsure>
        <FileVersion>3.2.0.0</FileVersion>
<!--
        <PolyArgumentExceptions>true</PolyArgumentExceptions>
-->
    </PropertyGroup>

    <PropertyGroup>
        <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
        <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
        <Squash_InternalNamespacesToKeep>CliInvoke</Squash_InternalNamespacesToKeep>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleToAttribute">
            <_Parameter1>CliInvoke.Tests</_Parameter1>
        </AssemblyAttribute>
        <!--
            Cross-package middleware consumption: CliInvoke.Specializations shell
            middleware must access internal rewriting helpers (ShellRewriter, enums,
            ArgumentTokenizer) and the derivation hook (ProcessConfigurationDerivation).
            Promotion to public rejected — no extensibility goal; a Specializations
            home impossible — no reference direction from Core. Justification per
            ADR-0001 (docs/adr/0001-ivt-minimization.md, Grant inventory:
            CliInvoke → CliInvoke.Specializations).
        -->
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="CliInvoke.Specializations"/>
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\CliInvoke.Core\CliInvoke.Core.csproj"/>
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions"/>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions"/>
        <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Caching.Memory"/>
        <PackageReference Include="Polyfill" PrivateAssets="all"/>
        <PackageReference Include="Squash" PrivateAssets="all"/>
        <PackageReference Include="Meziantou.Analyzer" PrivateAssets="all"/>
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <Content Include="..\..\README.md">
            <Link>README.md</Link>
            <PackagePath>README.md</PackagePath>
            <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
        </Content>
        <None Include="..\..\THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt">
            <Link>THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt</Link>
            <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
        </None>
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <EmbeddedResource Update="Internal\Localizations\Resources.resx">
            <Generator>ResXFileCodeGenerator</Generator>
            <LastGenOutput>Resources.Designer.cs</LastGenOutput>
        </EmbeddedResource>
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <Compile Update="Internal\Localizations\Resources.Designer.cs">
            <DesignTime>True</DesignTime>
            <AutoGen>True</AutoGen>
            <DependentUpon>Resources.resx</DependentUpon>
        </Compile>
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="..\..\.assets\icon.png">
            <Pack>True</Pack>
            <PackagePath>icon.png</PackagePath>
            <Link>icon.png</Link>
        </None>
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
